{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]The clickety sound of the [Bb]southbound [F]freight
[F]And the high speed hum of a passenger [C]train
[C]Becomes a part of the [F]soul and the [F/E]heart and the [Dm]mind
[Dm]Of a boy who's [Am]raised [C]by the railroad [F]line
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]The sound of a whistle at the [Bb]crossin' [F]road
[F]And the tanks and the trucks and the tractors on the flatcar [C]load
[C]Becomes a part of the [F]soul and the [F/E]heart and the [Dm]mind
[Dm]Of a boy who's [Am]raised [C]by the railroad [F]line
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]And the big round [Bb]penny that you [C]lay on the [Bb]rails
